<title>FRANCE: EU 96/97 grain exports seen at 26-27 mln T - AGPM.</title>
<headline>EU 96/97 grain exports seen at 26-27 mln T - AGPM.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French maize producers association AGPM expects the European Union to export around 26-27 million tonnes of grain by the end of the 1996/97 season, if it maintains its current export pace.</p>
<p>&quot;For the 1996/97 season, an ideal target would be 30 million tonnes but at the current (export) pace, export volume should be around 26-27 million tonnes,&quot; it said in a January newsletter, due for release later this week.</p>
<p>The European Union exported only 20 million tonnes of grain in 1995/96 (July/June) campaign when stocks were tight and prices high.</p>
<p>The latest EU statistics show EU grain export commitments between July 1, 1996 and January 29, 1997 stood at 18.65 million tonnes, up 40 percent over the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432 dom/bfl</p>
